 ],
 "notes": "Availability zone names are not pinned; region is a provider setting. alb_http_https_anywhere requires one TCP rule covering 80 through 443 (the prompt states a range); separate 80 and 443 rules do not satisfy it. sg_egress_only_vpc and internal_sgs_not_public enforce the 'limited to' and 'from the VPC CIDR' negatives; the rule-resource branches cannot tell which group a rule belongs to, and mixing inline and separate rules is not covered. Per-private-subnet route-table distinctness is approximated by route_tables (>=4): count-based association refs cannot distinguish instances. Per-port ingress checks require a TCP rule, so an all-protocol rule from the VPC CIDR does not stand in for a stated port. The six per-name existence checks were removed: six_sgs and the per-group port checks already require each named group. sg_egress_only_vpc's rule-resource branch cannot see inline egress, so a template mixing inline 0.0.0.0/0 egress with separate VPC egress rules would pass it (min-0 counts are not expressible)."
}